.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH miniserve 1  "miniserve 0.35.0" 
.SH "نام (NAME)"
miniserve \- For when you really just want to serve some files over HTTP right now!
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBminiserve\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-temp\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-index\fR] [\fB\-\-spa\fR] [\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-pretty\-urls\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interfaces\fR] [\fB\-\-workers\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-auth\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-route\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-\-random\-route\fR] [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-no\-symlinks\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-hidden\fR] [\fB\-S\fR|\fB\-\-default\-sorting\-method\fR] [\fB\-O\fR|\fB\-\-default\-sorting\-order\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-color\-scheme\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-color\-scheme\-dark\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-qrcode\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-upload\-files\fR] [\fB\-\-web\-upload\-files\-concurrency\fR] [\fB\-\-chmod\fR] [\fB\-\-directory\-size\fR] [\fB\-U\fR|\fB\-\-mkdir\fR] [\fB\-\-pastebin\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-media\-type\fR] [\fB\-M\fR|\fB\-\-raw\-media\-type\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-on\-duplicate\-files\fR] [\fB\-R\fR|\fB\-\-rm\-files\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-enable\-tar\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-enable\-tar\-gz\fR] [\fB\-z\fR|\fB\-\-enable\-zip\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-compress\-response\fR] [\fB\-D\fR|\fB\-\-dirs\-first\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-header\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-show\-symlink\-info\fR] [\fB\-F\fR|\fB\-\-hide\-version\-footer\fR] [\fB\-\-hide\-theme\-selector\fR] [\fB\-W\fR|\fB\-\-show\-wget\-footer\fR] [\fB\-\-print\-completions\fR] [\fB\-\-print\-manpage\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-readme\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-disable\-indexing\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\-webdav\fR] [\fB\-\-size\-display\fR] [\fB\-\-file\-external\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
For when you really just want to serve some files over HTTP right now!
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Be verbose, includes emitting access logs
.TP
\fB\-\-temp\-directory\fR \fI<TEMP_UPLOAD_DIRECTORY>\fR
The path to where file uploads will be written to before being moved to their correct location. It\*(Aqs wise to make sure that this directory will be written to disk and not into memory.

This value will only be used **IF** file uploading is enabled. If this option is not set, the operating system default temporary directory will be used.
.TP
\fB\-\-index\fR \fI<INDEX>\fR
The name of a directory index file to serve, like "index.html"

Normally, when miniserve serves a directory, it creates a listing for that directory. However, if a directory contains this file, miniserve will serve that file instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-spa\fR
Activate SPA (Single Page Application) mode

This will cause the file given by \-\-index to be served for all non\-existing file paths. In effect, this will serve the index file whenever a 404 would otherwise occur in order to allow the SPA router to handle the request instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Reduce output and silence warnings
.TP
\fB\-\-pretty\-urls\fR
Activate Pretty URLs mode

This will cause the server to serve the equivalent `.html` file indicated by the path.

`/about` will try to find `about.html` and serve it.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR [default: 8080]
Port to use
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interfaces\fR \fI<INTERFACES>\fR
Interface to listen on
.TP
\fB\-\-workers\fR \fI<WORKERS>\fR [default: 4]
Number of server workers
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-auth\fR \fI<AUTH>\fR
Set authentication

Currently supported formats:
username:password, username:sha256:hash, username:sha512:hash
(e.g. joe:123, joe:sha256:a665a45920422f9d417e4867efdc4fb8a04a1f3fff1fa07e998e86f7f7a27ae3)
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-file\fR \fI<AUTH_FILE>\fR
Read authentication values from a file

Example file content:

joe:123
bob:sha256:a665a45920422f9d417e4867efdc4fb8a04a1f3fff1fa07e998e86f7f7a27ae3
bill:
.TP
\fB\-\-route\-prefix\fR \fI<ROUTE_PREFIX>\fR
Use a specific route prefix
.TP
\fB\-\-random\-route\fR
Generate a random 6\-hexdigit route
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-no\-symlinks\fR
Hide symlinks in listing and prevent them from being followed
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-hidden\fR
Show hidden files
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-default\-sorting\-method\fR \fI<DEFAULT_SORTING_METHOD>\fR [default: name]
Default sorting method for file list
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
name: Sort by name
.IP \(bu 2
size: Sort by size
.IP \(bu 2
date: Sort by last modification date (natural sort: follows alphanumerical order)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-O\fR, \fB\-\-default\-sorting\-order\fR \fI<DEFAULT_SORTING_ORDER>\fR [default: desc]
Default sorting order for file list
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
asc: Ascending order
.IP \(bu 2
desc: Descending order
.RE
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-color\-scheme\fR \fI<COLOR_SCHEME>\fR [default: squirrel]
Default color scheme
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
squirrel
.IP \(bu 2
archlinux
.IP \(bu 2
ayu\-dark
.IP \(bu 2
zenburn
.IP \(bu 2
monokai
.RE
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-color\-scheme\-dark\fR \fI<COLOR_SCHEME_DARK>\fR [default: archlinux]
Default color scheme
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
squirrel
.IP \(bu 2
archlinux
.IP \(bu 2
ayu\-dark
.IP \(bu 2
zenburn
.IP \(bu 2
monokai
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-qrcode\fR
Enable QR code display
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-upload\-files\fR [\fI<ALLOWED_UPLOAD_DIR>\fR]
Enable file uploading (and optionally specify for which directory)

The provided path is not a physical file system path. Instead, it\*(Aqs relative to the serve dir. For instance, if the serve dir is \*(Aq/home/hello\*(Aq, set this to \*(Aq/upload\*(Aq to allow uploading to \*(Aq/home/hello/upload\*(Aq. When specified via environment variable, a path always needs to be specified.
.TP
\fB\-\-web\-upload\-files\-concurrency\fR \fI<WEB_UPLOAD_CONCURRENCY>\fR [default: 0]
Configure amount of concurrent uploads when visiting the website. Must have upload\-files option enabled for this setting to matter.

For example, a value of 4 would mean that the web browser will only upload 4 files at a time to the web server when using the web browser interface.

When the value is kept at 0, it attempts to resolve all the uploads at once in the web browser.

NOTE: Web pages have a limit of how many active HTTP connections that they can make at one time, so even though you might set a concurrency limit of 100, the browser might only make progress on the max amount of connections it allows the web page to have open.
.TP
\fB\-\-chmod\fR \fI<CHMOD>\fR
Set unix file permissions of uploaded files

This takes an octal number, for example 0600. By default 0666 & ~umask is used to simulate the system\*(Aqs default behavior.
.TP
\fB\-\-directory\-size\fR
Enable recursive directory size calculation

This is disabled by default because it is a potentially fairly IO intensive operation.
.TP
\fB\-U\fR, \fB\-\-mkdir\fR
Enable creating directories
.TP
\fB\-\-pastebin\fR
Enable creating pastebin \*(Aqpastes\*(Aq

\*(Aqpastes\*(Aq are plaintext files created in the current directory. Creation requires file uploads be enabled.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-media\-type\fR \fI<MEDIA_TYPE>\fR
Specify uploadable media types
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
image
.IP \(bu 2
audio
.IP \(bu 2
video
.RE
.TP
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-raw\-media\-type\fR \fI<MEDIA_TYPE_RAW>\fR
Directly specify the uploadable media type expression
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-on\-duplicate\-files\fR \fI<ON_DUPLICATE_FILES>\fR [default: error]
What to do if existing files with same name is present during file upload

If you enable renaming files, the renaming will occur by adding a numerical suffix to the filename before the final extension. For example file.txt will be uploaded as file\-1.txt, the number will be increased until an available filename is found.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
error
.IP \(bu 2
overwrite
.IP \(bu 2
rename
.RE
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-rm\-files\fR [\fI<ALLOWED_RM_DIR>\fR]
Enable file and directory deletion (and optionally specify for which directory)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-enable\-tar\fR
Enable uncompressed tar archive generation
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-enable\-tar\-gz\fR
Enable gz\-compressed tar archive generation
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-enable\-zip\fR
Enable zip archive generation

WARNING: Zipping large directories can result in out\-of\-memory exception because zip generation is done in memory and cannot be sent on the fly
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-compress\-response\fR
Compress response

WARNING: Enabling this option may slow down transfers due to CPU overhead, so it is disabled by default.

Only enable this option if you know that your users have slow connections or if you want to minimize your server\*(Aqs bandwidth usage.
.TP
\fB\-D\fR, \fB\-\-dirs\-first\fR
List directories first
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Shown instead of host in page title and heading
.TP
\fB\-\-header\fR \fI<HEADER>\fR
Inserts custom headers into the responses. Specify each header as a \*(AqHeader:Value\*(Aq pair. This parameter can be used multiple times to add multiple headers.

Example: \-\-header "Header1:Value1" \-\-header "Header2:Value2" (If a header is already set or previously inserted, it will not be overwritten.)
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-show\-symlink\-info\fR
Visualize symlinks in directory listing
.TP
\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-hide\-version\-footer\fR
Hide version footer
.TP
\fB\-\-hide\-theme\-selector\fR
Hide theme selector
.TP
\fB\-W\fR, \fB\-\-show\-wget\-footer\fR
If enabled, display a wget command to recursively download the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-completions\fR \fI<shell>\fR
Generate completion file for a shell
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash
.IP \(bu 2
elvish
.IP \(bu 2
fish
.IP \(bu 2
powershell
.IP \(bu 2
zsh
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-print\-manpage\fR
Generate man page
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR \fI<TLS_CERT>\fR
TLS certificate to use
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-key\fR \fI<TLS_KEY>\fR
TLS private key to use
.TP
\fB\-\-readme\fR
Enable README.md rendering in directories
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-disable\-indexing\fR
Disable indexing

This will prevent directory listings from being generated and return an error instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-webdav\fR
Enable read\-only WebDAV support (PROPFIND requests)
.TP
\fB\-\-size\-display\fR \fI<SIZE_DISPLAY>\fR [default: human]
Show served file size in exact bytes
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
exact
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-file\-external\-url\fR \fI<FILE_EXTERNAL_URL>\fR
Optional external URL (e.g., \*(Aqhttp://external.example.com:8081\*(Aq) prepended to file links in listings.

Allows serving files from a different URL than the browsing instance. Useful for setups like: one authenticated instance for browsing, linking files (via this option) to a second, non\-indexed (\-I) instance for direct downloads. This obscures the full file list on the download server, while users can still copy direct file URLs for sharing. The external URL is put verbatim in front of the relative location of the file, including the protocol. The user should take care this results in a valid URL, no further checks are being done.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-color\fR \fI<LOG_COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
Set the color style of the log output

"auto" (default) enables colors only when the output is a terminal. "always" always enables colors. "never" always disables colors.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Which path to serve
.SH "نسخه (VERSION)"
